## Replacement audio production set (CC0 sources)

`game/audio/paint_exe/` retains the replacement recordings, editable
scores/recipes and exported WAVs for POL#22. The game and Release ZIP use the
derived `game/content/sounds/paint_exe.xwb`, containing all 103 accepted masters.
Source files remain in the repository and are excluded from the ZIP. Exact per-file creators,
source URLs, licence evidence, modifications and hashes are recorded in
`game/audio/paint_exe/sources.json` and `game/audio/paint_exe/PROVENANCE.md`.

The source recordings are CC0 1.0 Universal, permitting both source redistribution
and use in the built bank/release. Voluntary credits: Joseph SARDIN (BigSoundBank),
OwlishMedia / owlstorm, unkleceeg, Mateusz Dąbrowski / FreePats, and Versilian
Studios LLC / VCSL. CC0 requires no attribution. The original ColourWars
arrangements and production code were authored with Codex and use this
repository's MIT licence; the source recordings retain their CC0 terms.

The author accepted this production set on 2026-10-14. The 2026-10-15 runtime
migration replaces the legacy game bindings and includes the replacement bank,
provenance and CC0 terms in the release. Further new cue hooks and in-game mix
acceptance remain open. If the optional bank is absent, the loader still
substitutes a silent bank, reports it once and lets the game continue.

## Content that is deliberately not distributed

### Retired legacy audio

The earlier `sound_bank_1` set is excluded from the repository and release.
Four of its twenty-four waves were commercial music tracks, and the remaining
waves had no retained source/licence records. Those files are not ColourWars'
to redistribute under MIT or any other licence. The roughly 154 MB PCM bank
and its sources also exceeded practical distribution limits. No legacy sample,
track, bank or timestamp-based reuse supplies the replacement bank.

### Fonts

`game/content/fonts/` holds compiled `.spritefont` files built from system
fonts (Gill Sans MT, Courier New) with Microsoft's `MakeSpriteFont`. The
compiled glyph atlases are redistributed here on the same footing as any other
game asset built from a licensed system font; the fonts themselves are not
included and are not ColourWars' to license.

### Menu artwork

`game/content/textures/menu_paint.png` is original artwork generated for
ColourWars using OpenAI image generation. The matching `.dds` is a lossless
RGBA conversion used at runtime; `menu_paint.json` defines its sprite frame.
The release includes the DDS and frame definition, while the PNG is retained
as the source artwork.
